-- COS 101 (Introduction to Computer Science, UNN) practice questions for the CBT feature.
-- Source: the official UNN Computer Science department textbook "Introduction to
-- Computer Science" (2016), cross-referenced against the official UNN COS 101
-- course outline's topic list (unn_computer_science_outline.sql) so every question
-- maps to a topic the student is actually meant to cover. All wording is original
-- (no verbatim textbook text reproduced), covering: hardware/software concepts,
-- computer subsystems and characteristics, input/output/storage devices, types of
-- computer, history and generations, algorithms/flowcharts/pseudocode, BASIC and
-- Java programming basics, booting/shutdown, operating system types, user
-- interface, malware/information management, computer networks, internet/web/
-- email/IM, office applications, statistical/database packages, and number
-- systems. Every explanation is a genuine step-by-step justification, not a bare
-- statement. Every field (question, options, explanation) is fully rendered in
-- LaTeX: every word is individually wrapped in its own $...$ span (prose in
-- \textrm{}), joined by literal spaces so MathText can still line-wrap normally --
-- matching the convention established for MTH 121.
--
-- Revised to fix two issues: (1) bare \text{} has no font override in
-- flutter_math_fork (only \textrm{}/\textnormal{} do), so every word was
-- silently rendering in math mode's italic letter font -- switched to \textrm{};
-- (2) the correct answer was frequently a full, detailed sentence while the three
-- distractors were short dismissive fragments ("a type of printer", "physically
-- damage the keyboard"), making the correct option identifiable by length alone
-- without knowing the content. Rewrote distractors across the bank to be
-- plausible, similarly-detailed alternatives at comparable length/register.
--
-- cbt_questions has no course_code column, so the COS 101 link lives in
-- subject_name. is_general = false and faculty/department are pinned to
-- 'Faculty of Physical Sciences' / 'Computer Science' so only students in that
-- faculty/department see this paper (same scoping principle used for MTH 121).

delete from public.cbt_questions where subject_id = 'cos-101-intro-computing';

insert into public.cbt_questions
  (subject_id, subject_name, institution, faculty, department, level,
   question, options, correct_index, explanation, topic, is_general)
